{
  "message": "I can help you with your phone's service issue. First, I need to verify your account. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, John. I have located your account. To help you with your 'No Service' issue, I’ll need to run a few quick checks on your line. Can you confirm if the phone number 555-123-2002 is the one experiencing the problem?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming. Your line appears to be active in our system, so let's troubleshoot your phone. Could you please check your phone's status bar and let me know if you see any icons like Airplane Mode, signal bars, or any other symbols? This will help me identify the cause of the 'No Service' message."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, the airplane icon means Airplane Mode is enabled, which turns off all wireless connections, including cellular service. Please turn off Airplane Mode on your phone. Once it's off, check if your signal bars reappear and let me know if you have service again."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for turning off Airplane Mode. Since you still see 'No Signal,' the next step is to check your SIM card. Please try removing your SIM card and then reinserting it to make sure it is properly seated. After you do this, let me know if your phone shows any signal bars or if the 'No Signal' message changes."
}

{
  "message": "You're doing everything right, and I appreciate your patience. Let's try another step. Sometimes, network settings can cause issues like this. Please restart your phone (turn it off and then back on). After it restarts, check if you have any signal bars or if the 'No Signal' message is gone. Let me know what you see after the restart."
}

{
  "message": "I understand how frustrating this is, and I want to reassure you that the steps we've taken so far—turning off Airplane Mode, reseating the SIM card, and restarting your phone—will not affect your photos or personal data. Your photos are safe. Since your line is active and these steps haven't resolved the issue, I will need to transfer you to a human agent for further assistance. Please hold on while I connect you."
}

{
  "message": "YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD ON."
}

{
  "message": "You're welcome, John. A human agent will assist you shortly. Thank you for your patience."
}

{
  "message": "I can help you with your MMS issue. First, I need to verify your identity. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for verifying your information, John. To help diagnose your MMS issue, could you please check if you are able to make regular calls and use mobile data (for example, browsing the web) on your phone? This will help determine if the problem is specific to MMS or related to your overall service or data connection."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please turn off Airplane Mode and try sending an MMS message again. Airplane Mode disables all wireless connections, including the ability to send MMS. Let me know if the issue persists after turning it off."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the update. The next step is to check if your messaging app has the necessary permissions to send MMS. Please grant the 'SMS' permission to your messaging app. Let me know once you have done this, or if you need instructions on how to do it."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for granting the SMS permission. The messaging app also needs permission to access your device's storage in order to send and receive MMS (pictures and videos). Please grant the 'storage' permission to your messaging app as well. Let me know once this is done or if you need help with the steps."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for updating the permissions. The next step is to check your phone's APN (Access Point Name) settings, as incorrect APN or missing MMSC URL can prevent MMS from working. Please check your APN settings and let me know if the MMSC URL is set, or if you see anything unusual. If you need instructions on how to check this, let me know."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking your APN settings. Let's try resetting your APN settings to default, as sometimes even correct-looking settings can have hidden issues. After resetting, please reboot your device for the changes to take effect. Let me know once you've completed these steps and if you are able to send MMS messages."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for following those steps. Next, let's check if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled on your device, as it can sometimes interfere with MMS. Please check your Wi-Fi Calling status and, if it is ON, turn it OFF. Let me know once you've done this or if you need instructions."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming that Wi-Fi Calling is off. Let's check your current network mode. MMS requires at least a 3G connection, and using 2G can cause issues. Please check your network mode preference and let me know if it is set to 2G, 3G, 4G, or 5G. If it is set to 2G, please change it to a mode that includes 3G, 4G, or 5G (such as '4G/5G preferred'). Let me know your current setting or if you need help with this step."
}

{
  "message": "Your network mode setting of '4G/5G preferred' is correct for MMS. Since we've checked permissions, APN settings, Wi-Fi Calling, and network mode, let's try one more thing: please run a speed test on your mobile data connection to ensure your data is working properly. Let me know the result of the speed test, especially if it shows 'no connection' or a very slow speed."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, if the speed test failed and shows 'No Connection,' it means your mobile data is not working, which is required for MMS. Let's troubleshoot your mobile data connection. First, please check if mobile data is enabled on your phone. If it is already enabled, let me know, and we can proceed to the next troubleshooting step."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming that mobile data is enabled and you have a strong signal. The next step is to check if Data Saver mode is turned on, as this can restrict your data connection. Please check your Data Saver status and let me know if it is enabled. If it is, please turn it off and try using mobile data again."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking Data Saver mode. Next, let's check if you are connected to a VPN, as this can sometimes interfere with mobile data. Please check your VPN status and let me know if a VPN is active. If it is, please disconnect from the VPN and try using mobile data again."
}

{
  "message": "It appears you have used 15.1GB of data this billing cycle, which is over your plan's 15GB data limit. This is likely why your mobile data and MMS are not working. You can add more data (up to 2GB) to restore your connection. Would you like to refuel your data now? The cost is $2.00 per GB."
}

{
  "message": "2GB of data has been successfully added to your line for $4.00. Please try using your mobile data and sending an MMS message again. If it still doesn't work, try rebooting your device. Let me know if you need any further assistance."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please reboot your device now. Rebooting can help your phone recognize the newly added data and restore your mobile data and MMS functionality. After rebooting, try sending an MMS message again and let me know if it works."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. Since we've tried all standard troubleshooting steps and your device, line, and account all appear to be in good standing, but MMS is still not working, this issue may require advanced technical support. I will transfer you to a human agent who can further assist you. Please hold on."
}

